# Without this, the entire repo (venv, node_modules, the 90MB wound
# dataset zip, the sqlite database) gets sent to the Docker daemon as
# build context on every build, even though the individual Dockerfiles
# only COPY specific directories into the image. Slow, and it means
# securederm.db briefly leaves the host even when nothing ever COPYs it.

.git/
.github/

venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/

datasets/
checkpoints/
logs/
backups/
wound_dataset/
wound_dataset.zip
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

docs/
README.md
